.\" Source: src/powers.c
.TH "POWERS" "1" "October 23, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
powers \- request spectrum measurements and print bin powers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B powers
.RI "[options] control-destination"
.SH DESCRIPTION
powers configures and polls a spectrum pseudo-demodulator in radiod and writes
frequency-bin powers as text. It uses the original floating-point spectrum
service, not spectrum2 byte responses. The command can create a dynamic
spectrum channel. It may change the demodulator of an existing channel if its
SSRC is reused; choose a dedicated SSRC.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-s ssrc, \-\-ssrc ssrc"
Select spectrum-channel SSRC. If omitted, the program chooses one.
.TP
.B "\-f frequency, \-\-frequency frequency"
Set center frequency; explicit SI suffixes are recommended.
.TP
.B "\-w Hz, \-\-bin\-width Hz"
Request resolution bandwidth in Hz. Specify a positive value for a new
channel.
.TP
.B "\-b count, \-\-bins count"
Request the number of frequency bins.
.TP
.B "\-a count, \-\-average count"
Set FFT averaging count. Default one.
.TP
.B "\-c count, \-\-count count"
Set number of output updates. Default one; -1 continues indefinitely.
.TP
.B "\-i seconds, \-\-interval seconds"
Set delay between completed updates. Default five seconds; acquisition time is
additional.
.TP
.B "\-T seconds, \-\-timeout seconds"
Set reply/retransmission timeout. Default one second.
.TP
.B "\-C Hz, \-\-crossover Hz"
Set crossover between wideband and narrowband spectrum algorithms. Default 200
Hz.
.TP
.B "\-d, \-\-details"
Print individual bin index, frequency, and dB power on separate lines instead
of one CSV record.
.TP
.B "\-o source, \-\-source source"
Restrict responses to one network source.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Increase diagnostics; repeat to dump protocol exchanges.
.TP
.B "\-V, \-\-version"
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
Print usage; currently exits nonzero.
.SH OUTPUT
Default output is a CSV-like record containing formatted GPS time, first and
last bin-center frequencies in Hz, bin spacing, number of bins, and one dB
power value per bin in increasing frequency order. It resembles rtl_power
output but is not an exact format guarantee. Zero-power bins are displayed at
the lowest nonzero power in that response. Values are bin powers under radiod
normalization, not automatically calibrated dBm/Hz.
.SH LIMITATIONS
--overlap appears in the long-option table but is not handled and is not
usable in this revision. Supply positive bandwidth and bin count when starting
a new spectrum channel. The utility retries on missing responses and may
continue waiting indefinitely.
.SH EXAMPLES
Request 100 bins around 10 MHz with 100 Hz resolution:
.PP
.nf
powers \-s 900001 \-f 10m \-w 100 \-b 100 \-a 10 hf.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), metadump(1), tune(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
